"""Deterministic builder of the A5 subsystem maturity matrix (fo_subsystem_maturity_matrix, M16).

    python docs/budgets/subsystem_maturity/build_subsystem_maturity.py           # write JSON + MD
    python docs/budgets/subsystem_maturity/build_subsystem_maturity.py --check   # verify the committed files

What it does. It reads the owner decisions A4/A5/A6 and the G0 baseline record (sha256-pinned, immutable) and the
verified repository deliverables listed in INPUTS (sha256 recorded in the output), and it writes the central execution
dashboard for the 16 A5 baseline subsystems plus the reserved RF pre-ionization module interface:
subsystem_maturity_v1.json (authoritative) and SUBSYSTEM_MATURITY.md (generated from it).

Evidence discipline (CLAUDE.md rules 3, 6, 10; docs/EVIDENCE.md).
* Subsystem names, allocations, requirement values and risk texts are read from their source files, not re-typed.
* Every curated statement carries at least one citation {path, locator, verified_tokens}. The builder checks that each
  cited file exists and contains every verified token (ids such as HW-H1-03, S1A-C1, D-09, DI-1.4 or quoted phrases);
  a missing token raises. Nothing is filled in: a missing input raises, it never falls back to a default.
* Premises that a row's blocker depends on (an owner decision still open, a readiness condition still MISSING, a W3
  requirement still TBD) are re-checked on every build; a changed premise raises so the row is revised, not silently
  kept.
* No allocation is invented: a sub-allocation appears only where A5 or A4 records one; everything else is
  TO_BE_ALLOCATED. No owner is invented: no accountable party is recorded in the inputs, so every owner cell is
  OWNER_TO_ASSIGN.

Parallel lanes (A6 execution: the four build lanes run simultaneously). The pre-ionizer ICD, the parametric Xe ledger
and the Phase-1 pre-registration framework do not exist in this lane's base. They are referenced by path as
"pending parallel lane <id>" and re-read lazily on every build: when their paths appear, the builder records the files
(sha256) and any declared top-level status, never their content; it never requires them.

Pure standard library plus abep_sim.arch_boundary (pure; read only). Runs in about a second. No Julia, no Hall model,
nothing wired into archengine, no golden moves.
"""
